          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em pullback
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distribution"} distribution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \in \mathcal{D}'(X)
            along a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon Y \to X
            is supposed to like the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \circ f
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            is thought of as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+function"} generalized function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            actually is an ordinary function.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            In general, the pullback of distributions along a smooth function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is meant to be a unique extension to distributions of the operation which on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bump+functions"} bump functions
            is given by pre-composition with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            If the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            we are pulling back along is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submersion"} submersion
          #PullbackOfDistributionAlongSubmersion.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (pullback of any distribution along a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submersion"} submersion
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1, X_2 \subset \mathbb{R}^n
              are two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \;\colon\; X_1 \overset{}{\longrightarrow} X_2
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submersion"} submersion
              (i.e. its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective+function"} surjective function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi x
